From 3accf2d76a76b3ac6e92c4c85b8fd2ab3dc09389 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 08:31:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 351/352] v2.2.3: rtrafd O(1) cli_slot index - fix the residual
 Traffic Analyzer stutter

The NCLI 64->192 bump in v2.2.2 tripled cli_slot()'s O(NCLI) linear scan, which
is called once per client-connection inside poll_fcache() (every 5 s, up to 1536
flows) and poll_conntrack(). On a 100+ client LAN that pushed the 5 s heavy tick
over the 100 ms budget -> an occasional micro-stutter in the live analyzer graph
that persists even with the v2.2.2 health probe OFF (probe-independent).

Fix: an open-addressed fnv(key)->slot hash index (cli_hash[512]) makes the common
path - a client we already track - a short hash probe instead of a full NCLI scan.
The index is maintained on the free-slot insert (cli_index_put), rebuilt on the
rare LRU eviction and on db restore (cli_index_rebuild), and cleared at startup;
cli_index_get re-checks the key so a hash collision can't false-match. New-client
allocation keeps its O(NCLI) free-slot walk (runs only on first sight of a client).

Scope: this is the probe-INDEPENDENT residual-stutter fix (plan item 0). The health
probe's own loop-blocking (conntrack parse + flash append + ICMP burst on the 10 Hz
tick) and the speed-test RT-throttle interaction remain for a follow-up (v2.2.4);
keep rtraf_hprobe=0 for now. See docs/V222-REGRESSION-PLAN.md.

BE96U MCP build owed (this commit) for owner testing.
